# Test fixture, not a build input.
#
# A handful of suites under tests/ parse SHAs out of a pins file to assert
# their own parsing logic and to name the commit their C++-as-text
# assertions are about (they read src/mod_overseer.cpp via the mod-overseer/
# submodule below). This is a vendored SNAPSHOT for that purpose only - it
# does not drive any build here.
#
# THE AUTHORITATIVE FILE lives in quadseven/infra at
# production/docker/azerothcore-playerbots/UPSTREAM-PINS.env, and it is the
# one that actually decides what quadseven/infra's AzerothCore image build
# clones. Keep AC_OVERSEER_SHA here equal to this repo's own mod-overseer/
# submodule pin (see .gitmodules / `git -C mod-overseer rev-parse HEAD`) - a
# mismatch between the two is exactly the drift infra#3093 was written to
# catch, just relocated: there it was pin-vs-gitlink-vs-checkout inside one
# repo, here it is this repo's submodule vs whatever infra separately pins.
# Nothing currently automates keeping AC_MODULE_SHA (mod-playerbots' own
# pinned commit) in sync with infra's copy; it is refreshed by hand when the
# tests that read it need a real value.
AC_OVERSEER_REPO=https://github.com/quadseven/mod-overseer.git
AC_OVERSEER_SHA=81277964a92bcf05c4c42facade1ea50065d678d
AC_MODULE_REPO=https://github.com/quadseven/mod-playerbots.git
AC_MODULE_SHA=60e6555e4e4b552ee4c6551b466aff648916f38b
